 "prompt": "Model a liquid-cooling cold plate with an internal serpentine channel (all dimensions in mm).\n- Block 120 along X, 80 along Y, 12 thick along Z, centred on the origin in X and Y, bottom on Z = 0.\n- Internal channel, rectangular section 8 wide x 4 high, between Z = 4 and Z = 8 (4 mm of material above and below).\n- The channel makes 5 straight passes along X, centred at Y = -28, -14, 0, 14, 28; channel centre lines run from X = -45 to X = 45.\n- Consecutive passes are joined by U-turns (square corners are acceptable), alternating ends: the first turn at X = +45 (between Y = -28 and -14), the next at X = -45, and so on.\n- Inlet port: vertical hole, diameter 8, from the top face down into the channel at (X = -45, Y = -28). Outlet port: same at (X = 45, Y = 28).\n- The channel must not break out of the block anywhere else.\n- Four through mounting holes, diameter 6.6, at (\u00b154, \u00b134).\nRequired PARAMS keys: length, width, thickness, channel_width, channel_height, channel_z, passes, pass_pitch, straight_half, port_d, mount_hole_d, mount_dx, mount_dy.",
